--------------------------------------------------
Requirement 1: Default Report Page Validation
--------------------------------------------------

Verify that the Report module displays the following:

Header:
- Generate Report

Select Report dropdown:
- Invoice Status Report
- Submission Report
- Reconciliation Report

Country:
- The Country field must display the country associated with the logged-in client user.
- Example: If the user belongs to a Belgium client, the field should display "Belgium".
- Do not hard-code Belgium unless the scenario explicitly uses Belgium test data.
- The expected country should come from the existing client or test-data configuration.

Entity:
- The default selected value must be "ALL" or the exact UI casing used by the application.
- Validate the actual product requirement if the UI displays "All" instead of "ALL".

Date or Date Range:
- The date inputs must display the placeholder "mm/dd/yyyy".
- If the application has separate start-date and end-date fields, validate both placeholders.
- If it uses a single date-range component, validate the placeholder according to the actual UI design.

Generate button:
- The Generate button must be disabled in the initial state.

--------------------------------------------------
Requirement 2: Generate Button State
--------------------------------------------------

Verify that the Generate button is enabled only after all mandatory inputs have valid values.

Mandatory values for applicable reports:

- Report type
- Entity
- Valid start date
- Valid end date
- Submission Platform, only for Submission Report

Example valid input:

- Report Type: Invoice Status Report
- Entity: ALL
- Start Date: 01/01/2025
- End Date: 10/10/2026

The feature should validate that the Generate button remains disabled when any mandatory field is missing or invalid.

At minimum, cover:

1. No report type selected.
2. Start date is missing.
3. End date is missing.
4. Date range is invalid because the start date is after the end date.
5. Submission Report is selected but Submission Platform is not selected.
6. All mandatory fields contain valid values.

Do not include unsupported negative cases if the application intentionally handles them differently. Clearly identify such cases as open questions.

